# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.pipeline.
#
# Pipeline image needs: processor/, replay/, loader/, and three files under
# docker/ (Dockerfile.pipeline, pipeline-entrypoint.sh, pipeline-requirements.txt).
# Everything else — the AZT1D + Shanghai datasets alone are ~900 MB — is
# excluded here so `docker build` doesn't ship it to the daemon or waste a
# GitHub Actions runner's upload budget.
#
# Blacklist style on purpose: dockerignore's `!dir/` re-inclusion rules
# interact badly with trailing slashes and prefix matching when you also
# want to re-include specific files inside a mostly-excluded directory.
# Explicit exclusions are easier to read and audit than a whitelist with
# five re-include lines.

# —— large data not needed at runtime (raw.readings_raw is already loaded on Azure) ——
data/

# —— analysis / scratch directories ——
scratch/
eval/
verification/
bench/

# —— offline / dev-only ——
tests/
docs/
scripts/
sql/

# —— different service, different image, deploys separately via App Service ——
dashboard/

# —— docker files that aren't part of the pipeline image ——
docker/Dockerfile.postgres
docker/pipeline-deploy.md

# —— repo / IDE metadata ——
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
.venv-deploy/
.gitignore
.env
.env.*

# —— project artefacts at root that the pipeline doesn't need ——
CLAUDE.md
Project1_CareVault_Plan_v2.pdf
docker-compose.yml
startup.sh
requirements.txt

# —— generated / stale files anywhere ——
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/*.log
**/*.swp
**/*.tmp
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
